r in Global Pharmaceutical and Biotech Management to join our Tutor Services Team at Coventry University Online (CUOL) delivering innovative, flexible and inclusive online education to a diverse global student community across our MSc postgraduate programmes. You will be focused on facilitating an engaging, inclusive and academically rigorous learning experience within a module-based online delivery model. The postholder will support students through a range of digital platforms primarily; Aula and Microsoft Teams. You will also contribute to the assessment, feedback and academic support activities that promote student progression, critical thinking and professional enhancement. This post offers an exciting opportunity for an experienced lecturer or industry practitioner to provide learning support in an exciting in a new and innovative mode of study to a diverse global student community. Qualifications Required Master’s degree in Biotechnology, Pharmaceutical Science, Bio-business, Innovation Management, or a closely aligned scientific/commercial discipline Our Successful Candidate You will possess a strong understanding of science in order to contextualise teaching and bridge between scientific innovation and commercial execution. The post holder will be comfortable using technology to enable effective support to both large/small cohorts of students at distance, utilising the Aula platforms. This position is ideal for an experienced practitioner with a passion for online education, digital innovation, and widening participation in higher education. The Benefits As a member of Coventry University Online, you will have access to a wide range of industry leading rewards and benefits which includes: Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual Leave plus 8 days Bank Holidays Holiday Purchase Scheme 50% off Tuition Fees for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/Online Retailers Cycle to Work Scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded within the fabric of our organisation and are a key focus of our core values. We harness the power and potential of the diverse cultures, backgrounds, abilities, and experiences of our students, colleagues, and partners to create opportunities for all. Full Job Description & Person Specification Click here to view the full job description and person specification We look forward to hearing from you! Please enable JavaScript Screen readers cannot read the following searchable map. Follow this link to reach our Job Search page to search for available jobs in a more accessible format. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Online Coventry Home View All Jobs Website Privacy Notice Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Confirm My Choices Accept All Cookies"
