    "https://cugcareers.coventry.ac.uk/job/Coventry-Associate-Lecturer-in-Psychology-Applied-Psychology-Cove-CV1/1371980457/": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer in Psychology / Applied Psychology Job Details",
      "description": "Associate Lecturer in Psychology / Applied Psychology Job Details | coventryun We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Locations Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Faculty/Business Area All Location All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Job Title Associate Lecturer in Psychology / Applied Psychology Job Reference 3741 Application Closing Date 27/09/2026 Division, Department Coventry University Online Limited (CUOL) ,CUOL Operations Salary £34.85 per hour Mode Hourly Paid, Fixed Term until 31/08/2027 Our Mission Coventry University is a global Education Group with a mission of Creating Better Futures. Driven by our passion and belief that through education, equity, and innovation our students, people, and communities are empowered to transform their lives and the world around them. This role is based within Coventry University Online Learning, a sister company of Coventry University and part of the Coventry University Group. The Role We are seeking an Associate Lecturer in Applied Psychology / Psychology to join our Tutor Services Team in delivering innovative, flexible and inclusive online education to a diverse global student community across our MSc Psychology programmes. As Associate Lecturer you will be focused on facilitating an engaging, inclusive and academically rigorous learning experience within a module-based online delivery model. The postholder will support students through a range of digital platforms primarily; Aula and Microsoft Teams. You will support students by providing constructive feedback on assignments, and encouraging active, independent learning. This role requires an ability to create a challenging, thought-provoking learning environment that promotes debate and develops the students’ analytical skills. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced lecturer to contribute to a diverse and global student community in an innovative, fully online learning environment. Qualifications Required Master’s degree in Applied Psychology or similar field (this must be a qualification in psychology) Our Successful Candidate We are looking for a subject expert in Applied Psychology & Psychology, with a relevant qualification in the field. The ideal candidate will have experience teaching Applied Psychology & Psychology at postgraduate level and be committed to supporting students in developing their critical thinking, academic skills, and understanding of the subject. You will have High level of proficiency in ICT and understanding of its application to teaching and learning support and committed to delivering high quality services to students and external clients This position is ideal for an experienced practitioner with a passion for online education, digital innovation, and widening participation in higher education. The Benefits As a member of Coventry University Online, you will have access to a wide range of industry leading rewards and benefits which includes: Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual Leave plus 8 days Bank Holidays Holiday Purchase Scheme 50% off Tuition Fees for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/Online Retailers Cycle to Work Scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded within the fabric of our organisation and are a key focus of our core values. We harness the power and potential of the diverse cultures, backgrounds, abilities, and experiences of our students, colleagues, and partners to create opportunities for all. Full Job Description & Person Specification Click here to view the full job description and person specification We look forward to hearing from you! Please enable JavaScript Screen readers cannot read the following searchable map. Follow this link to reach our Job Search page to search for available jobs in a more accessible format. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Online Coventry Home View All Jobs Website Privacy Notice Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visit