sic Psychology and Mental health to join Coventry University Online. As Associate Lecturer will utilise the virtual learning platform Aula to deliver quality driven learning to a cohort of online students, ensuring engagement and academic development throughout modules. You will support students by providing constructive feedback on assignments, and encouraging active, independent learning. This role requires an ability to create a challenging, thought-provoking learning environment that promotes debate and develops the students’ analytical skills. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced lecturer to contribute to a diverse and global student community in an innovative, fully online learning environment. Qualifications Required Master’s degree in forensic psychology & mental health or similar field (this must be a qualification in psychology) Our Successful Candidate The ideal candidate will have experience teaching forensic psychology & mental health at postgraduate level and be committed to supporting students in developing their critical thinking, academic skills, and understanding of the subject. You will have High level of proficiency in ICT and understanding of its application to teaching and learning support and committed to delivering high quality services to students and external clients This post is a thrilling opportunity for an experienced lecturer to deliver learning support in an exciting and new mode of study to a wealth of students from a global community. The Benefits As a member of Coventry University Online, you will have access to a wide range of industry leading rewards and benefits which includes: Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual Leave plus 8 days Bank Holidays Holiday Purchase Scheme 50% off Tuition Fees for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/Online Retailers Cycle to Work Scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded wit