    "https://cugcareers.coventry.ac.uk/job/Scarborough-Assistant-Professor-%28Teaching%29-in-Occupational-Therapy-Scar-YO11-2JW/1372427757/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Teaching) in Occupational Therapy Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Teaching) in Occupational Therapy Job Details | coventryun We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Locations Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Faculty/Business Area All Location All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Job Title Assistant Professor (Teaching) in Occupational Therapy Job Reference 3677 Application Closing Date 09/10/2026 Division, Department CUHC CU Health and Care Limited (CUHC) ,AHP Occupational Therapy Salary Competitive starting salary range from £46,761 up to £53,333 per annum (dependent upon experience) with the potential to progress. A discretionary range for candidates with exceptional experience can be discussed/considered. Mode Permanent , Full Time Our Mission Coventry University Group is a global education provider dedicated to Creating Better Futures. We are driven by the belief that through education, equity, and innovation, we empower our students, people, and communities to transform their lives. Central to our 2030 Strategy is the ambitious growth of our School of Health and Care to meet current and evolving health and care needs locally, nationally, and globally. To enable this, our School has evolved into Coventry University Health and Care Limited. This agile, autonomous structure allows us to push boundaries and foster closer partnerships, enabling us to scale our provision and widen access to rewarding careers across the health and social care sector. The Role An exciting opportunity has arisen to join our thoughtful and dedicated occupational therapy team as an Assistant Professor (Teaching). Our well-established pre-registration courses, delivered across different campus sites, offer a range of routes into the profession including direct entry and apprenticeships; undergraduate and postgraduate. Our focus is on developing reflective, compassionate, and highly skilled occupational therapists, whilst fostering excellence, innovation, and supervision in occupational therapy education and training. Duties include Course leadership and coordination. Directing the curation, adaptation, design and development of module and course teaching materials and contributing to ongoing curriculum development, including practice-based learning. Teaching on modules and courses at HE levels 4-7 and our Level 6 occupational therapist apprenticeship, and leading teams of teaching staff. Leading moderation and quality assurance of appropriate module assessment. Line management Liaison with external stakeholders as required, including employers and practice partners Qualifications Required Essential Current registration with the HCPC as an occupational therapist Master’s degree in a relevant subject OR (if from a professional practice background) a good Honors Degree and an appropriate professional qualification and/or membership A teaching qualification or acceptance of the requirement to undertake one if not already held Experience of delivering occupational therapy education (professional/university/apprenticeship) Desirable PhD Active membership of an appropriate professional body Our Successful Candidate You will have demonstrable experience of successful teaching at higher education levels 4-7 in occupational therapy and/or the Level 6 occupational therapist apprenticeship. You will have experience of leading on curriculum design and delivery and can demonstrate best practice in teaching, learning and assessment consistent with our reputation and track record as a high-quality provider of teaching and learning. An experienced team leader with good level of digital fluency, you will have experience using creating teaching materials for face to face and online teaching using a VLE. Enthusiastic and self-motivated, you will have experience in the development and enhancement of an ‘active learning’ pedagogy as appropriate to the academic subject area. As a global education provider, high levels of cultural awareness with experience of learner’s cultural differences and expectations with the ability to effectively communicate with a wide range of people from diverse backgrounds is essential. Innovation and collaboration are key to our success, therefore the ability to generate and follow through innovative ideas, work both independently and part of a wider team with the willingness to engage in flexible ways of working are key skills required for this role. Contact: Dr Tracey Rehling (Associate Professor in Occupational Therapy and Associate Head of Department for Allied Health Professions). Email: ac8183@coventry.ac.uk Please contact me to discuss how your professional experience to date could align with the job description and person specification. Don’t be put off by the language of Higher Education Institutes – you could be exactly the person we are looking for to help educate the future occupational therapy workforce! The Benefits As a staff member, you will have access to a wide range of industry-leading rewards and benefits which include: Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual leave plus Bank Holidays New Holiday Purchase Scheme up to 5 additional days Life Assurance 4x Salary BUPA Cash Plan 50% off Tuition Fees for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/ Online Retailers Cycle To Work scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded within the fabric of our organisation and are a key focus of our core values. We harness the power and potential of the diverse cultures, backgrounds, abilities, and experiences of our students, colleagues, and partners to create opportunities for all. Full Job and Person Specification Click here to view the full job description and person specification We look forward to hearing from you! Please enable JavaScript Screen readers cannot read the following searchable map. Follow this link to reach our Job Search page to search for available jobs in a more accessible format. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Coventry Home View All Jobs Website Privacy Notice Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary) prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Confirm My Choices Accept All Cookies"
