    "https://cugcareers.coventry.ac.uk/job/London-Assistant-Lecturer-%28Teaching%29-in-Adult-Nursing-Lond-Se15/1372580857/": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer (Teaching) in Adult Nursing Job Details",
      "description": "Assistant Lecturer (Teaching) in Adult Nursing Job Details | coventryun We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Locations Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Faculty/Business Area All Location All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Job Title Assistant Lecturer (Teaching) in Adult Nursing Job Reference 3821 Application Closing Date 08/10/2026 Division, Department CUHC CU Health and Care Limited (CUHC) ,CUHC Nursing and Midwifery (NM) Salary Competitive starting salary range from £33,403 up to £37,606 pro rata (dependent on experience) with the potential to progress. A discretionary range for candidates with exceptional experience can be discussed/considered. Mode Permanent , Part Time Our Mission Coventry University Health and Care (CUHC), a sister company of Coventry University, provides a sector leading, dedicated inclusive service to Coventry University Group students supporting their successful global education experience and graduate employment outcomes. Tailoring our service to each students’ individual needs and career aspirations, we are an integral part of the student journey that starts at enrolment and continues beyond graduation. Our dedicated Teaching team are subject specialists focused on delivering student education, which is active, social, applied, and inclusive within our vibrant and varied education environment. This role offers an exciting opportunity to join our team as an Assistant Lecturer (Teaching) in Adult Nursing. The Role As an Assistant Lecturer (Teaching) in Adult Nursing you will undertake teaching and assessment activities and act as a practice education link tutor to support to our placement partnership within London and Greater London areas. Based onsite at Coventry University in London, Vauxhall Campus, you will work closely with other academic colleagues to enrich the student learning and teaching experience to ensure, as appropriate, relevant aspects of research, enterprise and professional context are embedded in modules and courses. Duties include: Teaching on modules and courses at HE levels 4, 5, 6 and 7 in relevant academic subject areas. Teaching will predominantly be related to clinical nursing skills delivery. Supporting the design, implementation, ratification and quality assurance processes related to student assessment. Upholding high standards of academic integrity in all aspects of teaching, learning and assessment The preparation and dissemination of both generic and specific formative and summative student feedback. Conducting student placement visits as a link tutor across our London and Greater London practice placements. Undertaking the role of Academic Assessor The development and demonstration of best practice in teaching, learning and assessment consistent with our reputation and track record as a high-quality provider of teaching and learning. The development and enhancement of an active learning pedagogy as appropriate to the academic subject area. Qualifications Required NMC Registration in Nursing (Current and Active) as an adult nurse is essential for this role. Practice Assessor training. An Honours Degree in an appropriate/ relevant subject area with professional qualification. A teaching qualification or acceptance of the requirement to acquire one if not already held. A PhD, or a Master's Degree would be advantageous. Our Successful Candidate You will have demonstrable experience of successful teaching at higher education levels 4-7 in Adult Nursing either within Higher Education or within the clinical practice environment. You will have strong evidence of supporting student learning within the clinical environment as a practice assessor and have a good working knowledge of the NMC SSSA Standards. You can demonstrate a high standard of teaching, learning and student engagement consistent with our reputation and track record as a high-quality provider of teaching and learning. You will have a passion for sharing knowledge and supporting students in their learning journey, both in clinical practice and in the classroom, with the ability to work flexibly to meet learner needs. Enthusiastic and self-motivated, you will have experience supporting, enhancing and engaging in an ‘active learning’ pedagogy with evidence in proactively supporting student success. As a global education provider, experience and awareness of learners cultural differences and expectations with the ability to effectively communicate with a wide range of people from diverse backgrounds is essential. Innovation and collaboration are key to our success, therefore the ability to work both independently and part of a wider team with the willingness to engage in flexible ways of working are key skills required for this role The Benefits As a staff member of Coventry University, you will have an access to a wide range of industry leading rewards and benefits which includes: Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual leave plus Bank Holidays New Holiday Purchase Scheme up to 5 additional days Life Assurance 4 x Salary BUPA Cash Plan 50% off Tuition Fees for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/ Online Retailers Cycle To work scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded within the fabric of our organisation and are a key focus of our core values. We harness the power and potential of the diverse cultures, backgrounds, abilities, and experiences of our students, colleagues, and partners to create opportunities for all. If you would like an informal discussion about this role please contact Emma Winterman: ae2433@coventry.ac.uk Full Job Description & Person Specification Click here to view the full job description and person specification We look forward to hearing from you! Please enable JavaScript Screen readers cannot read the following searchable map. Follow this link to reach our Job Search page to search for available jobs in a more accessible format. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Coventry Home View All Jobs Website Privacy Notice Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data centre \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the