    "https://cugcareers.coventry.ac.uk/job/Coventry-Tutor-in-Languages-Cove-CV1/1372680057/": {
      "title": "Tutor in Languages Job Details",
      "description": "Tutor in Languages Job Details | coventryun We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve the website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Accept All Cookies Skip to main content View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Our Locations View profile Career Opportunities Our Culture Application Process Rewards and Benefits Locations Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Category All Faculty/Business Area All Location All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Job Title Tutor in Languages Job Reference 3774 Application Closing Date 05/10/2026 Division, Department CUG Academic ,CUG School of Languages Salary Competitive starting salary range from £41,049 up to £42,286 pro rata (dependent on experience) with the potential to progress. A discretionary range for candidates with exceptional experience can be discussed/considered. Mode Part Time, Fixed Term until 18/12/2026 Our Mission Coventry University Group is a global education group with a mission of Creating Better Futures. We are driven by our passionate belief in the transformational power of education and research to enable and empower our students, colleagues and partners and to improve the world around them. Our people are key to our success, and each role contributes to the Group’s ongoing progress in communities around the world. The Role We are looking to recruit an EAP Tutor experienced in language test delivery to oversee the administration of the Coventry University English Test (CUET). The CUET is an English language proficiency test delivered in person in various international locations as part of relationship building with partner institutions and overall student recruitment strategy for the University. The postholder will manage a team of markers, including leading standardisation of marking.  They will liaise with the CU Recruitment & Admissions team (CURA) to allocate existing test materials to particular test events, make these materials available to invigilators under the agreed procedures to maintain security, and manage the allocation of completed tests for marking to the marking team. They will be responsible for ensuring marking is completed and returned to CURA within agreed timelines, for moderation of all marking, and will deal with any issues around test breaches or academic misconduct. They will also train the in-person test invigilators in the agreed test procedures, including maintaining test security. Further details: 18.5 hours per week (0.5fte) Contract dates: 5 October to 18 December 2026, with the potential for further contracts for key student recruitment cycles in 2027. Remote work – the successful candidate will not need to attend the Coventry campus but will need to be based within the UK and be available remotely during working hours to liaise with stakeholders and markers. Qualifications Required Undergraduate degree Diploma level qualification and/or Masters in a relevant subject (e.g. TESOL, Applied Linguistics, Language Testing) Native or near native speaker (IELTS 8.0 or above) standard of written and spoken English Our Successful Candidate The successful candidate will have an understanding of secure test processes and procedures, as well as language testing principles. Experience of managing secure language test delivery, standardisation and moderation of marking, interpreting English language descriptors, and dealing with academic misconduct within language test settings They will have led teaching or marking teams previously and will have experience of cross-team working and liaison with stakeholders in other areas of an education institution. They will have strong organisational skills to manage marking for multiple test events within a specific testing cycle, as well as strong attention to detail and demonstrable accuracy in data reporting. They will also be thoroughly familiar with processes around data security, confidentiality and GDPR. The Benefits As a staff member of CU Group, you will have access to a wide range of industry leading rewards and benefits. Excellent Employers Pension Contribution 30 days Annual leave plus Bank Holidays New Holiday Purchase Scheme up to 5 additional days Life Assurance 4 x Salary BUPA Cash Plan 50% off Tuition Fees for staff dependants CU Reward Scheme – Discounts across a range of High Street/ Online Retailers Cycle To work scheme Our Culture As a global Education Group, equality, diversity, and inclusion are embedded within the fabric of our organisation and are a key focus of our core values. We harness the power and potential of the diverse cultures, backgrounds, abilities, and experiences of our students, colleagues, and partners to create opportunities for all. Full Job Description & Person Specification Click here to view the full job description and person specification We look forward to hearing from you! Please enable JavaScript Screen readers cannot read the following searchable map. Follow this link to reach our Job Search page to search for available jobs in a more accessible format. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Coventry Coventry Home View All Jobs Website Privacy Notice Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. × Cookie Consent Manager When you vis